<<<
For synonyms in the sense scope or purview, see FIELD. By SLIPSHOD EXTENSION, the word is often now made to mean a person to whom r. is permitted as a witness to character, & even a written testimonial.
===
For synonyms in the sense *scope* or *purview*, see ^^FIELD^^. By ^^SLIPSHOD EXTENSION^^, the word is often now made to mean a person to whom *r.* is permitted as a witness to character, & even a written testimonial.
>>>

<<<
referendum, properly meaning a question to be referred (to the people), has been appropriated as a name for the system of so referring questions & for any particular occasion of its exercise; the normal form would have been reference, but referendum has the advantage over that of not bearing several other senses. The plural -da is better avoided as too suggestive (cf. memoranda, agenda, &c.) of the correct sense—questions to be referred— ; use -ms.
===
**referendum,** properly meaning a question to be referred (to the people), has been appropriated as a name for the system of so referring questions & for any particular occasion of its exercise; the normal form would have been *reference*, but *referendum* has the advantage over that of not bearing several other senses. The plural *-da* is better avoided as too suggestive (cf. *memoranda, agenda,* &c.) of the correct sense—questions to be referred—; use *-ms*.
>>>

